    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1605">

                <pb facs="1336" n="1232" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg1232"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 723.2515/289.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the American Minister
                        to Peru.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-03-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 17, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department encloses for your strictly
                    confidential information a copy of a despatch from the Legation at Santiago,
                    dated January 30, 1913, relative to the possible settlement of the Tacna <pb
                        facs="1337" n="1233" xml:id="pg1233"/> Arica dispute, and a copy of the
                    Department’s reply to Minister Fletcher.</p>
                <p>You will be guided in general by the instruction to Mr. Fletcher, but should any
                    situation as that indicated in the instruction arise, you will, before
                    committing this Government, telegraph for special instructions.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
